    "type": "mc",
    "text": "<div style=\"text-align:center; margin:1.2em 0;\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 300 210\" class=\"dx-fig\" role=\"img\" style=\"color:var(--text);max-width:280px;\"><title>Right triangle ABC with the right angle at B; AB is 8 units and BC is 15 units</title><polygon points=\"80,50 80,175 245,175\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><polyline points=\"80.0,163.0 92.0,163.0 92.0,175.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\"><tspan font-style=\"italic\">A</tspan></text><text x=\"68\" y=\"189\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\"><tspan font-style=\"italic\">B</tspan></text><text x=\"249\" y=\"189\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\"><tspan font-style=\"italic\">C</tspan></text><text x=\"62\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"currentColor\">8</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\">15</text></svg></div>Note: Figure not drawn to scale.<br><br>In the figure, triangle <i>ABC</i> has a right angle at <i>B</i>, the length of <i>AB</i> is 8 units, and the length of <i>BC</i> is 15 units. Which of the following must be true?<br><br>I. The measure of angle <i>A</i> is greater than the measure of angle <i>C</i>.<br>II. sin <i>A</i> = <span style=\"display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch;vertical-align:middle;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0.12em;font-size:0.95em;\"><span style=\"border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;padding:0 0.25em;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;\">8</span><span style=\"padding:0 0.25em;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;\">17</span></span>",
    "choices": [
     "I only",
     "II only",
     "I and II",
     "Neither I nor II"
    ],
    "correct": 0,
    "explanation": "Choice A is correct. By the Pythagorean theorem <i>AC</i> = √(8<sup>2</sup> + 15<sup>2</sup>), which is √(64 + 225), or √289, so <i>AC</i> = 17 units. Statement I is true. In any triangle the larger angle lies opposite the longer side. The side opposite angle <i>A</i> is <i>BC</i>, which is 15 units, and the side opposite angle <i>C</i> is <i>AB</i>, which is 8 units, so angle <i>A</i> is the larger of the two. Statement II is not true. The sine of an acute angle in a right triangle is the length of the side opposite that angle divided by the length of the hypotenuse. The side opposite angle <i>A</i> is <i>BC</i>, so sin <i>A</i> = <span style=\"display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch;vertical-align:middle;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0.12em;font-size:0.95em;\"><span style=\"border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;padding:0 0.25em;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;\">15</span><span style=\"padding:0 0.25em;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;\">17</span></span>. The ratio <span style=\"display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch;vertical-align:middle;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0.12em;font-size:0.95em;\"><span style=\"border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;padding:0 0.25em;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;\">8</span><span style=\"padding:0 0.25em;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;\">17</span></span> is sin <i>C</i>, and it is also cos <i>A</i>.<br><br>Choice B is incorrect. Statement I is true, since angle <i>A</i> lies opposite the longer leg, <i>BC</i>. Statement II is not true: the ratio 8 to 17 is sin <i>C</i>, not sin <i>A</i>.<br><br>Choice C is incorrect. Statement II is not true. The side opposite angle <i>A</i> is <i>BC</i>, which is 15 units, so sin <i>A</i> is the ratio 15 to 17.<br><br>Choice D is incorrect. Statement I is true. In any triangle the larger angle lies opposite the longer side, and the side opposite angle <i>A</i> is longer than the side opposite angle <i>C</i>.",
    "source": "Moretti Test Prep & Tutoring"
