    "text": "<div style=\"text-align:center; margin:1.2em 0; font-size:1.1em;\"><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse; margin:0 auto;\" border=\"1\"><tr><th style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">Time, <i>t</i> (minutes)</th><th style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">Temperature, <i>T</i> (°C)</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">0</td><td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">18</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">2</td><td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">30</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">4</td><td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">42</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">6</td><td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\">54</td></tr></table></div>A pot of water was placed on a stove, and the burner under the pot was turned on. The table shows the temperature <i>T</i>, in degrees Celsius (°C), of the water <i>t</i> minutes after the burner was turned on. During this time, the temperature of the water increased at a constant rate. Which equation represents the relationship between <i>T</i> and <i>t</i>?",
